      <div type="clause" n="26">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 26</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">[Be mansworum.] [Ld] Ond se ðe manað swerige, ⁊ hit him on open wurðe, ðæt he næfre eft æðwyrþe ne sy, ne binnon nanum gehalgodum lictune ne licge, þeah he forðfore, buton he hæbbe ðæs biscopes gewitnesse, ðe he on his scriftscire sy, þæt he hit swa gebet hæbbe, swa him his scrift scrife.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">And if anyone swears a false oath and it becomes manifest he has done so, he shall never again have the right to swear an oath; and he shall not be buried in any consecrated burial ground when he dies, unless he has the testimony of the bishop, in whose diocese he is, that he has made such amends as his confessor has prescribed for him.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Be mansworum. Se ðe mænne aþ swerige, ⁊ hit him on open weorþe, þæt he næfre æþwyrþe ne sy, ne binnan nanum gehalgodum lictune ne licge, ðeah he gefære, butan he hæbbe ðæs bisceopes gewitnysse, ðe he on his scire sy, þæt he hit swa gebete hæbbe, swa his scrift him scrife.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
